>CDD:107203 cd01560, Thr-synth_2, Threonine synthase catalyzes the final 
step of threonine biosynthesis. The conversion of O-phosphohomoserine 
into threonine and inorganic phosphate is pyridoxal 
5'-phosphate dependent. The Thr-synth_1 CD includes members 
from higher plants, cyanobacteria, archaebacteria and eubacterial 
groups. This CD, Thr-synth_2, includes enzymes from 
fungi and eubacterial groups, as well as, metazoan threonine 
synthase-like proteins.
