>CDD:396757 pfam02321, OEP, Outer membrane efflux protein.  The OEP family 
(Outer membrane efflux protein) form trimeric channels that 
allow export of a variety of substrates in Gram negative bacteria. 
Each member of this family is composed of two repeats. 
The trimeric channel is composed of a 12 stranded all beta 
sheet barrel that spans the outer membrane, and a long all 
helical barrel that spans the periplasm.
