Z, type 1.  FtsZ is a GTPase that is similar to the eukaryotic 
tubulins and is essential for cell division in prokaryotes. 
 FtsZ is capable of polymerizing in a GTP-driven process 
into structures similar to those formed by tubulin. FtsZ forms 
a ring-shaped septum at the site of bacterial cell division, 
which is required for constriction of cell membrane and 
cell envelope to yield two daughter cells.
