>CDD:214867 smart00864, Tubulin, Tubulin/FtsZ family, GTPase domain.  This 
domain is found in all tubulin chains, as well as the bacterial 
FtsZ family of proteins. These proteins are involved in 
polymer formation. Tubulin is the major component of microtubules, 
while FtsZ is the polymer-forming protein of bacterial 
cell division, it is part of a ring in the middle of the 
dividing cell that is required for constriction of cell membrane 
and cell envelope to yield two daughter cells. FtsZ and 
tubulin are GTPases, this entry is the GTPase domain. FtsZ 
can polymerise into tubes, sheets, and rings in vitro and is 
ubiquitous in bacteria and archaea.
